WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.936
(audience cheering)

00:00:00.936 --> 00:00:02.264
- It's nice to see you.

00:00:02.264 --> 00:00:03.182
- It's so nice to see you too.

00:00:03.182 --> 00:00:05.152
- I was asked several
times if we'd ever met,

00:00:05.152 --> 00:00:05.985
and I was like,

00:00:05.985 --> 00:00:06.818
"I don't think so."

00:00:06.818 --> 00:00:07.670
- We've met three times.

00:00:07.670 --> 00:00:08.503
- [Kelly] No, we have not.

00:00:08.503 --> 00:00:09.336
- No, I'm kidding.

00:00:09.336 --> 00:00:10.169
- Oh my God.

00:00:10.169 --> 00:00:11.002
I was like, "Oh my God."

00:00:11.002 --> 00:00:11.835
I was like-

00:00:11.835 --> 00:00:12.668
- They asked me the same

00:00:12.668 --> 00:00:13.859
and I feel like we have,

00:00:13.859 --> 00:00:15.208
but I just feel like-

00:00:15.208 --> 00:00:16.468
- It might have been in passing then,

00:00:16.468 --> 00:00:17.367
because they asked me too.

00:00:17.367 --> 00:00:18.200
They always ask me

00:00:18.200 --> 00:00:19.120
because I've been in the industry

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:20.013
doing other things, right?

00:00:20.013 --> 00:00:20.846
- [Jake] Yes.

00:00:20.846 --> 00:00:22.264
- So I'm like, "I don't think so."

00:00:22.264 --> 00:00:23.097
But I don't know,

00:00:23.097 --> 00:00:24.447
it might have been in
passing or something.

00:00:24.447 --> 00:00:25.757
But if you don't really remember

00:00:25.757 --> 00:00:27.235
and I don't remember-

00:00:27.235 --> 00:00:28.198
- Then we definitely have.

00:00:28.198 --> 00:00:29.243
- Maybe we just see each other in things

00:00:29.243 --> 00:00:30.076
and we're like,

00:00:30.076 --> 00:00:30.909
"We know each other."

00:00:30.909 --> 00:00:31.742
- Yeah, no,

00:00:31.742 --> 00:00:32.575
I think I see you on TV.

00:00:32.575 --> 00:00:33.408
You have a TV show, right?

00:00:33.408 --> 00:00:34.269
- Yeah, little bit.

00:00:34.269 --> 00:00:35.319
- Okay, I think maybe that's probably it.

00:00:35.319 --> 00:00:36.299
- Yeah, that's probably it, yeah.

00:00:36.299 --> 00:00:37.326
Do you ever do that, by the way?

00:00:37.326 --> 00:00:38.333
Have you ever run into someone

00:00:38.333 --> 00:00:39.166
and you're like,

00:00:39.166 --> 00:00:39.999
you think you know them

00:00:39.999 --> 00:00:40.832
and then you figure out

00:00:40.832 --> 00:00:42.453
they're someone in a film or something?

00:00:42.453 --> 00:00:43.457
- Oh, always.

00:00:43.457 --> 00:00:45.044
- [Kelly] Okay, that's
totally happened to me.

00:00:45.044 --> 00:00:45.877
- All the time.

00:00:45.877 --> 00:00:46.710
- I didn't say anything, but like,

00:00:46.710 --> 00:00:47.970
I was in an elevator and I was like,

00:00:47.970 --> 00:00:50.080
"I- Nope, you don't know that person."

00:00:50.080 --> 00:00:52.120
And it's like, don't say anything,

00:00:52.120 --> 00:00:53.118
you don't know them.

00:00:53.118 --> 00:00:54.480
Wait, I just mentioned "City Slickers"

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:56.110
which is one of my favorite movies.

00:00:56.110 --> 00:00:57.311
I know it's a long time ago for you.

00:00:57.311 --> 00:00:58.144
- That's never been mentioned

00:00:58.144 --> 00:01:00.052
on anything I've ever-

00:01:00.052 --> 00:01:01.015
- Are you serious?

00:01:01.015 --> 00:01:01.848
- [Jake] Yeah.

00:01:01.848 --> 00:01:03.873
It's very rarely talked
about in the oeuvre,

00:01:03.873 --> 00:01:05.224
you know what I mean?

00:01:05.224 --> 00:01:06.057
- I thought I was going to be

00:01:06.057 --> 00:01:07.053
that annoying person that asks you

00:01:07.053 --> 00:01:08.393
about the films you're
asked about all the time

00:01:08.393 --> 00:01:09.690
since you were a kid, okay.

00:01:09.690 --> 00:01:10.855
- I mean, kind of.

00:01:10.855 --> 00:01:13.663
It's a very special movie
for me because it's-

00:01:13.663 --> 00:01:15.879
- Me, too, I love that movie so much.

00:01:15.879 --> 00:01:16.712
- [Jake] Yeah.

00:01:16.712 --> 00:01:17.545
- And I just thought it was so crazy.

00:01:17.545 --> 00:01:18.532
So how did you end up doing that movie?

00:01:18.532 --> 00:01:20.081
You were young, right?

00:01:20.081 --> 00:01:22.120
- I was 11, yeah.

00:01:22.120 --> 00:01:22.953
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:01:22.953 --> 00:01:23.786
- [Jake] I know,

00:01:23.786 --> 00:01:24.619
it's the first thing I ever did was,

00:01:24.619 --> 00:01:25.452
I was 11 years old.

00:01:25.452 --> 00:01:26.398
- [Kelly] Your first thing ever to do

00:01:26.398 --> 00:01:27.681
was with that cast?

00:01:27.681 --> 00:01:28.514
- Yeah.

00:01:28.514 --> 00:01:29.347
- [Kelly] Sure.

00:01:29.347 --> 00:01:30.354
- Pretty incredible, I know.

00:01:30.354 --> 00:01:31.682
Well, it's weird.

00:01:31.682 --> 00:01:32.515
- Life.

00:01:32.515 --> 00:01:33.901
It's like, wow.

00:01:33.901 --> 00:01:34.984
- Well it's weird

00:01:34.984 --> 00:01:37.530
because my parents made movies

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:38.363
and you know,

00:01:38.363 --> 00:01:39.375
my mother's a writer

00:01:39.375 --> 00:01:40.593
and so there was a night

00:01:40.593 --> 00:01:44.845
Billy Crystal was
actually at our house and-

00:01:44.845 --> 00:01:45.678
Yeah, yeah,

00:01:45.678 --> 00:01:47.762
and I was 10 or something like that.

00:01:47.762 --> 00:01:50.555
And at the end of dinner
everyone was leaving

00:01:50.555 --> 00:01:52.444
and I was just so enamored by him,

00:01:52.444 --> 00:01:53.279
you know, like I was like,

00:01:53.279 --> 00:01:54.467
"Oh my God, it's Billy."

00:01:54.467 --> 00:01:55.300
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:01:55.300 --> 00:01:56.237
- And I just picked up a chair

00:01:56.237 --> 00:01:59.252
and I offered it to him as a parting gift.

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.519
(audience laughs)

00:02:00.519 --> 00:02:02.187
I was like, "Here's a party favor."

00:02:02.187 --> 00:02:03.430
I like handed him the chair,

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:05.730
and he thought it was so funny,

00:02:05.730 --> 00:02:08.379
and I was just wanting
to give him a chair.

00:02:08.379 --> 00:02:10.035
- Just genuine, like, "Take this."

00:02:10.035 --> 00:02:10.868
- I just didn't know what,

00:02:10.868 --> 00:02:11.701
you know when someone's like,

00:02:11.701 --> 00:02:12.534
and you just want to give them something

00:02:12.534 --> 00:02:13.367
and you're like,

00:02:13.367 --> 00:02:14.685
"Just take, take it."

00:02:14.685 --> 00:02:15.535
You know what I mean?

00:02:15.535 --> 00:02:17.139
And that's how I was and he loved it.

00:02:17.139 --> 00:02:18.258
- "A souvenir of this dinner."

00:02:18.258 --> 00:02:19.091
- Basically.

00:02:19.091 --> 00:02:19.924
And he was like,

00:02:19.924 --> 00:02:21.248
"That kid's got something special."

00:02:21.248 --> 00:02:22.821
(Kelly laughs)

00:02:22.821 --> 00:02:24.042
Little did he know, but yeah.

00:02:24.042 --> 00:02:25.342
- Oh my God, that's amazing.

00:02:25.342 --> 00:02:26.175
- He was like, "Come audition

00:02:26.175 --> 00:02:27.491
for this new movie that I'm doing

00:02:27.491 --> 00:02:29.019
because I need someone to play my son."

00:02:29.019 --> 00:02:30.188
And then I did,

00:02:30.188 --> 00:02:31.147
and then I got the part.

00:02:31.147 --> 00:02:31.980
- [Kelly] That's so cool.

00:02:31.980 --> 00:02:32.813
- Yeah.

00:02:32.813 --> 00:02:33.646
- Did you ever have any real jobs,

00:02:33.646 --> 00:02:34.479
like regular jobs?

00:02:34.479 --> 00:02:35.312
(Jake laughing)

00:02:35.312 --> 00:02:36.483
Like I mean,

00:02:36.483 --> 00:02:37.902
wait for it.

00:02:37.902 --> 00:02:39.239
I just heard it.

00:02:39.239 --> 00:02:40.352
- No, no, no, no.

00:02:40.352 --> 00:02:41.185
No, no,

00:02:41.185 --> 00:02:42.605
it makes total sense, by the way-

00:02:42.605 --> 00:02:44.097
- I mean, like, in life,

00:02:44.097 --> 00:02:45.409
like a normal average-

00:02:45.409 --> 00:02:46.991
I've had a lot of like normal jobs.

00:02:46.991 --> 00:02:48.256
- You're just digging-

00:02:48.256 --> 00:02:49.089
No, no, of course.

00:02:49.089 --> 00:02:49.922
You're right.

00:02:49.922 --> 00:02:50.755
- Being an actor is not-

00:02:50.755 --> 00:02:51.588
You play, it's fun.

00:02:51.588 --> 00:02:52.853
It's being a musician, same thing.

00:02:52.853 --> 00:02:53.686
- Yeah, I agree.

00:02:53.686 --> 00:02:54.519
- Yeah.

00:02:54.519 --> 00:02:55.352
Not fake, but-

00:02:55.352 --> 00:02:56.270
- Yeah. But we do.

00:02:56.270 --> 00:02:57.103
No, but I mean,

00:02:57.103 --> 00:02:59.271
I'm not like actually playing someone,

00:02:59.271 --> 00:03:00.334
I'm not in the military,

00:03:00.334 --> 00:03:01.167
I'm not actually playing,

00:03:01.167 --> 00:03:02.816
I'm not that thing,

00:03:02.816 --> 00:03:03.649
I'm playing it.

00:03:03.649 --> 00:03:05.384
So it is a little not real, but-

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:07.064
- [Kelly] I just meant like a normal job.

00:03:07.064 --> 00:03:07.998
- I got it.

00:03:07.998 --> 00:03:09.528
- Like I worked at Papa John's, man.

00:03:09.528 --> 00:03:10.966
You ever worked at Papa John's?

00:03:10.966 --> 00:03:11.799
- No, it's fine.

00:03:11.799 --> 00:03:12.632
No, I didn't work at 'Papa John's',

00:03:12.632 --> 00:03:14.715
but I was a lifeguard.

00:03:14.715 --> 00:03:15.673
- Oh.

00:03:15.673 --> 00:03:18.135
No, that's another real job.

00:03:18.135 --> 00:03:18.968
(audience applauds)

00:03:18.968 --> 00:03:19.801
- They're excited about that.

00:03:19.801 --> 00:03:20.712
- That's another real job.

00:03:20.712 --> 00:03:21.903
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:03:21.903 --> 00:03:24.054
- Wait, did you ever save anyone's life?

00:03:24.054 --> 00:03:25.976
- Well, in a way, yeah.

00:03:25.976 --> 00:03:27.860
- What does this mean?

00:03:27.860 --> 00:03:28.693
- Well, like, I didn't,

00:03:28.693 --> 00:03:31.669
I wasn't like "Baywatch" necessarily.

00:03:31.669 --> 00:03:33.152
It was more like,

00:03:33.152 --> 00:03:34.764
I guarded the beach.

00:03:34.764 --> 00:03:36.691
Like meaning there was like a public beach

00:03:36.691 --> 00:03:37.559
and a private beach

00:03:37.559 --> 00:03:38.910
and I had to tell people

00:03:38.910 --> 00:03:41.191
to not come onto the private beach.

00:03:41.191 --> 00:03:42.024
- Oh.

00:03:42.024 --> 00:03:42.857
(audience laughing)

00:03:42.857 --> 00:03:43.926
You were the person to remind them

00:03:43.926 --> 00:03:45.645
of what level they were at.

00:03:45.645 --> 00:03:47.490
(audience laughs)

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.587
"You haven't made it here.

00:03:49.587 --> 00:03:50.804
These are the fake people

00:03:50.804 --> 00:03:51.958
with the fake jobs."

00:03:51.958 --> 00:03:54.152
- "The people who are
having fun over here,

00:03:54.152 --> 00:03:55.042
you're not allowed there."

00:03:55.042 --> 00:03:56.852
But like, it was more like,

00:03:56.852 --> 00:03:58.865
it was just like a mark guy,

00:03:58.865 --> 00:04:00.317
just a boundary marker, you know?

00:04:00.317 --> 00:04:01.211
And I most of the time

00:04:01.211 --> 00:04:02.604
just had to get up and be like,

00:04:02.604 --> 00:04:03.437
"Sorry,"

00:04:03.437 --> 00:04:05.038
and then people were
just pissed, you know?

00:04:05.038 --> 00:04:05.871
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:05.871 --> 00:04:07.868
You were like a beach bouncer.

00:04:07.868 --> 00:04:08.701
- Basically.

00:04:08.701 --> 00:04:09.660
That's exactly what I was.

00:04:09.660 --> 00:04:10.493
- Yeah.

00:04:10.493 --> 00:04:11.326
- That's better actually.

00:04:11.326 --> 00:04:12.159
That's what I should have said.

00:04:12.159 --> 00:04:12.992
- Sounds cool.

00:04:12.992 --> 00:04:14.270
- Yeah, but then I also
had to do other things

00:04:14.270 --> 00:04:15.922
like first aid and stuff like that.

00:04:15.922 --> 00:04:16.755
- [Kelly] That's cool.

00:04:16.755 --> 00:04:17.588
- Yeah, that was cool.

00:04:17.588 --> 00:04:18.421
- I actually took a class,

00:04:18.421 --> 00:04:19.590
like I know how to do CPR.

00:04:19.590 --> 00:04:21.317
I enjoy learning stuff like that, do you?

00:04:21.317 --> 00:04:22.287
- I do too, it's really important.

00:04:22.287 --> 00:04:23.120
- [Kelly] Yeah.

00:04:23.120 --> 00:04:23.953
- I think it's really important.

00:04:23.953 --> 00:04:24.870
- Yeah, I think it's when I had kids.

00:04:24.870 --> 00:04:25.982
I was like, "Don't die,"

00:04:25.982 --> 00:04:26.994
I did everything to learn

00:04:26.994 --> 00:04:28.609
for them not to die.

00:04:28.609 --> 00:04:29.442
- That's a good plan.

00:04:29.442 --> 00:04:30.275
- Yeah.

00:04:30.275 --> 00:04:31.201
I feel like I'm killing it.

00:04:31.201 --> 00:04:32.452
- Yeah.

00:04:32.452 --> 00:04:33.422
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:33.422 --> 00:04:34.255
Killing it?

00:04:34.255 --> 00:04:35.396
- Um.

00:04:35.396 --> 00:04:37.956
(Kelly laughs)

00:04:37.956 --> 00:04:38.926
- I respect that,

00:04:38.926 --> 00:04:41.748
you're hardworking at your normal job.

00:04:41.748 --> 00:04:43.798
- At your normal job.

00:04:43.798 --> 00:04:47.114
(audience laughs)

00:04:47.114 --> 00:04:48.769
At your real job.

00:04:48.769 --> 00:04:50.945
At my fake one, we just do this.

00:04:50.945 --> 00:04:51.904
- But the thing is, is that,

00:04:51.904 --> 00:04:52.849
like one time

00:04:52.849 --> 00:04:54.957
somebody got stung by a jellyfish,

00:04:54.957 --> 00:04:55.901
like a man o' war.

00:04:55.901 --> 00:04:57.056
- Ooh, I've been stung by a jellyfish.

00:04:57.056 --> 00:04:57.889
- It's no fun.

00:04:57.889 --> 00:04:58.722
- Yeah.

00:04:58.722 --> 00:04:59.935
- Like a big one or like a tiny one?

00:04:59.935 --> 00:05:00.821
- I don't know how big it was,

00:05:00.821 --> 00:05:01.654
but it hurt like hell

00:05:01.654 --> 00:05:03.305
and I had to pee on myself.

00:05:03.305 --> 00:05:04.171
(audience laughs)

00:05:04.171 --> 00:05:05.148
Yeah, they were like,

00:05:05.148 --> 00:05:05.981
"You gotta pee on herself,"

00:05:05.981 --> 00:05:06.814
and everybody's like,

00:05:06.814 --> 00:05:07.647
"She's not gonna be able to do it,"

00:05:07.647 --> 00:05:08.616
and I was like, going.

00:05:08.616 --> 00:05:09.688
(audience laughs)

00:05:09.688 --> 00:05:13.070
I was like, "Will it take away the burn?

00:05:13.070 --> 00:05:16.907
I will pee on in front
of anyone if it will-"

00:05:16.907 --> 00:05:18.181
- That's what I decided-

00:05:18.181 --> 00:05:19.990
- You peed on yourself or someone?

00:05:19.990 --> 00:05:21.123
- Well, they told me that

00:05:21.123 --> 00:05:22.328
that was what you had to do

00:05:22.328 --> 00:05:23.456
and a person was in pain.

00:05:23.456 --> 00:05:26.661
(everyone laughing)

00:05:26.661 --> 00:05:29.661
(audience cheering)

00:05:31.103 --> 00:05:34.020
I suggested that we should use pee,

00:05:35.198 --> 00:05:36.448
I suggested it.

00:05:38.183 --> 00:05:39.544
And they, at that point,

00:05:39.544 --> 00:05:42.177
you know the pain of a jellyfish sting,

00:05:42.177 --> 00:05:43.393
they wanted it,

00:05:43.393 --> 00:05:44.721
they'd take anything, really.

00:05:44.721 --> 00:05:46.684
- They couldn't pee themselves, huh?

00:05:46.684 --> 00:05:48.418
- Well, I didn't really pee on them.

00:05:48.418 --> 00:05:49.501
- [Kelly] Oh, okay.

00:05:49.501 --> 00:05:51.742
- We sort of took some pee in.

00:05:51.742 --> 00:05:52.780
- Okay.

00:05:52.780 --> 00:05:54.403
- It was their choice.

00:05:54.403 --> 00:05:57.309
(Kelly laughing)

00:05:57.309 --> 00:05:58.320
- I just love this.

00:05:58.320 --> 00:06:00.261
- You do what you need to sometimes

00:06:00.261 --> 00:06:01.240
to save a life,

00:06:01.240 --> 00:06:02.226
you know what I mean?

00:06:02.226 --> 00:06:03.677
(audience cheering)

00:06:03.677 --> 00:06:05.353
- So before the break,

00:06:05.353 --> 00:06:06.855
we were talking about your job,

00:06:06.855 --> 00:06:07.947
your real job,

00:06:07.947 --> 00:06:09.094
as a lifeguard,

00:06:09.094 --> 00:06:10.887
but you were also a sous chef as well.

00:06:10.887 --> 00:06:12.596
Do you still love to cook?

00:06:12.596 --> 00:06:13.657
- I love cooking, yes.

00:06:13.657 --> 00:06:16.762
- Can you get me into
that idea, that theme?

00:06:16.762 --> 00:06:17.619
- That you like cooking?

00:06:17.619 --> 00:06:18.452
- Yeah.

00:06:18.452 --> 00:06:19.609
I just really want to like it.

00:06:19.609 --> 00:06:20.442
And I go in there,

00:06:20.442 --> 00:06:21.606
and there's like two things I make

00:06:21.606 --> 00:06:22.914
that I'm like, "Cool."

00:06:22.914 --> 00:06:23.747
But like,

00:06:23.747 --> 00:06:25.174
I just really wanna be into it.

00:06:25.174 --> 00:06:26.554
What got you into it?

00:06:26.554 --> 00:06:27.395
- I think,

00:06:27.395 --> 00:06:28.705
well my family all cooked together

00:06:28.705 --> 00:06:29.623
when I was a kid.

00:06:29.623 --> 00:06:30.456
- Oh, well.

00:06:30.456 --> 00:06:31.645
- And my dad did a lot of cooking,

00:06:31.645 --> 00:06:32.581
and my mom did too.

00:06:32.581 --> 00:06:35.614
My dad did mostly the warm food cooking

00:06:35.614 --> 00:06:37.568
and my mom did the cold food cooking.

00:06:37.568 --> 00:06:39.354
Like, she would make a killer salad

00:06:39.354 --> 00:06:41.883
and then my dad would make like,

00:06:41.883 --> 00:06:42.922
you know,

00:06:42.922 --> 00:06:43.841
protein or whatever.

00:06:43.841 --> 00:06:44.674
- [Kelly] Steak.

00:06:44.674 --> 00:06:45.757
- Steak, yeah.

00:06:45.757 --> 00:06:49.257
But we always got along best at the table,

00:06:50.250 --> 00:06:51.083
you know?

00:06:51.083 --> 00:06:52.002
It was like the conversations we'd have

00:06:52.002 --> 00:06:53.148
and the food, we all love food.

00:06:53.148 --> 00:06:55.164
So I started to just love it.

00:06:55.164 --> 00:06:56.319
I don't really know where it came from.

00:06:56.319 --> 00:06:57.911
I just love eating.

00:06:57.911 --> 00:06:58.895
So then I was like-

00:06:58.895 --> 00:07:01.008
- Well, I'm into that part.

00:07:01.008 --> 00:07:02.159
I love that part.

00:07:02.159 --> 00:07:03.888
I just, I can't-

00:07:03.888 --> 00:07:04.904
I'm trying,

00:07:04.904 --> 00:07:06.708
and we do so many cooking
things on the show.

00:07:06.708 --> 00:07:07.541
- Yeah.

00:07:07.541 --> 00:07:08.374
- And I'm trying to get into it,

00:07:08.374 --> 00:07:09.207
but every time I get in there I'm like,

00:07:09.207 --> 00:07:10.253
"Or I could read."

00:07:10.253 --> 00:07:11.282
- [Jake] You don't have to.

00:07:11.282 --> 00:07:12.357
This is the thing.

00:07:12.357 --> 00:07:13.974
I think that there's a
lot of pressure on that-

00:07:13.974 --> 00:07:14.807
- I could have wine.

00:07:14.807 --> 00:07:15.640
- Yeah.

00:07:15.640 --> 00:07:17.383
I do think there's a lot of pressure

00:07:17.383 --> 00:07:19.822
on needing to be able to cook somehow.

00:07:19.822 --> 00:07:20.731
And I don't know what it is.

00:07:20.731 --> 00:07:22.091
And you gotta love it.

00:07:22.091 --> 00:07:23.069
- I feel like I might.

00:07:23.069 --> 00:07:24.437
Are you healthier though because of it?

00:07:24.437 --> 00:07:25.270
That's why,

00:07:25.270 --> 00:07:26.325
I feel like people that I know that cook

00:07:26.325 --> 00:07:27.947
are generally really healthy.

00:07:27.947 --> 00:07:28.780
- Yeah.

00:07:28.780 --> 00:07:30.340
- I'm not like a shiny example of that.

00:07:30.340 --> 00:07:31.277
So like, I think-

00:07:31.277 --> 00:07:32.110
- You're not healthy?

00:07:32.110 --> 00:07:33.028
- No.

00:07:33.028 --> 00:07:34.253
I eat really good things

00:07:34.253 --> 00:07:36.080
but I also really love bad things.

00:07:36.080 --> 00:07:36.913
- Yeah.

00:07:36.913 --> 00:07:38.905
But you can cook bad things.

00:07:38.905 --> 00:07:40.125
- And like with good ingredients?

00:07:40.125 --> 00:07:41.053
- Well, if you love something

00:07:41.053 --> 00:07:42.226
you can be like, "Oh, I love this thing

00:07:42.226 --> 00:07:43.552
and then I'm gonna find the ingredients."

00:07:43.552 --> 00:07:44.385
It doesn't have to be
really good ingredients,

00:07:44.385 --> 00:07:45.218
you just start cooking it

00:07:45.218 --> 00:07:46.051
and then you're like, "Oh,

00:07:46.051 --> 00:07:46.884
I'm gonna try it this way

00:07:46.884 --> 00:07:47.717
and try it that way,"

00:07:47.717 --> 00:07:48.550
and then you just do it differently

00:07:48.550 --> 00:07:49.534
and then it changes stuff.

00:07:49.534 --> 00:07:50.367
You know?

00:07:50.367 --> 00:07:51.200
- I have tried several times

00:07:51.200 --> 00:07:52.033
with healthy ingredients,

00:07:52.033 --> 00:07:53.963
and sometimes I'm like, "No."

00:07:53.963 --> 00:07:55.035
- No. Yeah.

00:07:55.035 --> 00:07:56.069
It's funny you say that

00:07:56.069 --> 00:07:59.097
'cause I tried to bake
this thing the other day

00:07:59.097 --> 00:08:00.485
that's in this amazing-

00:08:00.485 --> 00:08:01.318
- I love baking.

00:08:01.318 --> 00:08:02.151
- Yeah. Baking.

00:08:02.151 --> 00:08:02.984
- I do love baking.

00:08:02.984 --> 00:08:03.817
Not cooking.

00:08:03.817 --> 00:08:04.650
- Well, it's sort of the same-

00:08:04.650 --> 00:08:05.483
- Different.

00:08:05.483 --> 00:08:06.316
- I mean, it's sort of-

00:08:06.316 --> 00:08:07.149
- Different.

00:08:07.149 --> 00:08:09.229
- [Jake] I'm not gonna
argue with you there.

00:08:09.229 --> 00:08:10.494
I feel like that's a very sensitive-

00:08:10.494 --> 00:08:11.577
- It takes no thought.

00:08:11.577 --> 00:08:12.817
- That's not true.

00:08:12.817 --> 00:08:13.695
- No, I feel like it's-

00:08:13.695 --> 00:08:15.574
- All the bakers in the
world just went like,

00:08:15.574 --> 00:08:16.585
"It takes no thought?"

00:08:16.585 --> 00:08:17.664
- No, it takes like-

00:08:17.664 --> 00:08:18.668
(audience laughs)

00:08:18.668 --> 00:08:20.037
"You're in a fake job."

00:08:20.037 --> 00:08:20.870
- Yeah.

00:08:20.870 --> 00:08:22.019
"You fake baker!"

00:08:22.019 --> 00:08:23.216
- I feel like because with cooking

00:08:23.216 --> 00:08:25.703
you're like, a dab, a splash of,

00:08:25.703 --> 00:08:26.536
you know, a pinch.

00:08:26.536 --> 00:08:27.868
And I'm like, that's relative.

00:08:27.868 --> 00:08:29.709
- Oh, meaning you need measurements.

00:08:29.709 --> 00:08:30.542
- [Kelly] I need the chemistry.

00:08:30.542 --> 00:08:32.418
- What's fake about that?

00:08:32.418 --> 00:08:34.475
And all the scientists hate you too now.

00:08:34.475 --> 00:08:36.176
- I need the recipe

00:08:36.176 --> 00:08:37.230
and I can follow it to tee

00:08:37.230 --> 00:08:38.352
and I'm good at baking.

00:08:38.352 --> 00:08:39.185
- Yeah.

00:08:39.185 --> 00:08:40.204
I mean, I understand.

00:08:40.204 --> 00:08:41.453
I think baking's really hard.

00:08:41.453 --> 00:08:42.474
I think it's harder than that.

00:08:42.474 --> 00:08:43.504
- Oh, I love baking.

00:08:43.504 --> 00:08:44.429
- [Jake] Well, there we go.

00:08:44.429 --> 00:08:45.262
- I'm good at that, okay.

00:08:45.262 --> 00:08:46.095
- [Jake] Now we got a competition.

00:08:46.095 --> 00:08:46.928
- What did you bake though?

00:08:46.928 --> 00:08:48.595
- I baked this like,

00:08:50.732 --> 00:08:53.573
flowerless chocolate meringue cake.

00:08:53.573 --> 00:08:54.595
- Ooh, I love meringue.

00:08:54.595 --> 00:08:55.835
- [Jake] From this amazing
book by this woman,

00:08:55.835 --> 00:08:56.668
Claire Saffitz.

00:08:56.668 --> 00:08:57.824
- Meringue is hard.

00:08:57.824 --> 00:08:58.657
- Yeah.

00:08:58.657 --> 00:08:59.659
- [Kelly] Oh, shut up.

00:08:59.659 --> 00:09:02.492
(audience laughs)

00:09:03.354 --> 00:09:04.335
- No.

00:09:04.335 --> 00:09:05.831
- Meringue is so hard for me.

00:09:05.831 --> 00:09:06.664
- I mean-

00:09:06.664 --> 00:09:07.497
- I screw it up.

00:09:07.497 --> 00:09:08.330
- How do you do it?

00:09:08.330 --> 00:09:09.897
- Not well.

00:09:09.897 --> 00:09:11.702
- Do you use an electric mixer

00:09:11.702 --> 00:09:13.810
or do you use a whisk?

00:09:13.810 --> 00:09:14.993
- I've done both.

00:09:14.993 --> 00:09:15.826
I've done both.

00:09:15.826 --> 00:09:16.720
I literally lost a competition

00:09:16.720 --> 00:09:18.497
to my tour manager once on a pie

00:09:18.497 --> 00:09:19.754
because of the meringue.

00:09:19.754 --> 00:09:21.479
It was a sad meringue.

00:09:21.479 --> 00:09:22.312
- Really?

00:09:22.312 --> 00:09:23.264
- Yeah.

00:09:23.264 --> 00:09:24.097
What did you do, though?

00:09:24.097 --> 00:09:25.260
Did you use like a healthy ingredient

00:09:25.260 --> 00:09:26.211
that didn't work out or something?

00:09:26.211 --> 00:09:27.044
- Well, yeah, I tried.

00:09:27.044 --> 00:09:27.877
- That's what I did.

00:09:27.877 --> 00:09:28.710
- I tried coconut sugar,

00:09:28.710 --> 00:09:30.495
which is just a real no-go

00:09:30.495 --> 00:09:31.600
for an egg white.

00:09:31.600 --> 00:09:34.069
Sometimes you just need the bad stuff.

00:09:34.069 --> 00:09:35.062
You just need regular sugar.

00:09:35.062 --> 00:09:36.304
- I do like monk fruit.

00:09:36.304 --> 00:09:37.170
I dunno if you've ever used that.

00:09:37.170 --> 00:09:38.003
- Monk fruit's wonderful.

00:09:38.003 --> 00:09:38.836
I love monk fruit.

00:09:38.836 --> 00:09:39.669
Yeah.

00:09:39.669 --> 00:09:40.869
You need to go for,

00:09:40.869 --> 00:09:42.506
you know, real sugar,

00:09:42.506 --> 00:09:45.438
it really makes those
stiff peaks, you know?

00:09:45.438 --> 00:09:46.971
And that's what you need for a meringue,

00:09:46.971 --> 00:09:47.804
you know what I mean?

00:09:47.804 --> 00:09:48.637
- I used real sugar,

00:09:48.637 --> 00:09:50.931
I just sucked at it.

00:09:50.931 --> 00:09:52.291
So your new movie,

00:09:52.291 --> 00:09:54.958
since you're not an actual chef-

00:09:55.911 --> 00:09:57.151
- Or do anything normal.

00:09:57.151 --> 00:09:57.984
Yeah, it's fine.

00:09:57.984 --> 00:09:58.817
No big deal.

00:09:58.817 --> 00:10:00.200
- Since you have no real job.

00:10:00.200 --> 00:10:01.146
- It was hard to walk out here.

00:10:01.146 --> 00:10:03.561
I don't how I got out here.

00:10:03.561 --> 00:10:04.760
- I'm so sorry.

00:10:04.760 --> 00:10:05.753
So your new movie,

00:10:05.753 --> 00:10:06.941
it's called "The Covenant".

00:10:06.941 --> 00:10:08.194
So can you tell everybody what it's about?

00:10:08.194 --> 00:10:09.027
- [Jake] Yeah.

00:10:09.027 --> 00:10:10.742
It's a story about

00:10:10.742 --> 00:10:12.929
a special operations sergeant

00:10:12.929 --> 00:10:15.732
and an Afghan interpreter

00:10:15.732 --> 00:10:17.647
who sort of become

00:10:17.647 --> 00:10:19.730
likely kind of connected.

00:10:21.461 --> 00:10:24.413
And basically it's a story
about repaying a debt.

00:10:24.413 --> 00:10:25.246
You know?

00:10:25.246 --> 00:10:27.413
It's a story about one guy

00:10:29.257 --> 00:10:30.626
who does something for the other one,

00:10:30.626 --> 00:10:31.680
basically saves his life,

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:33.661
and in the end, you know,

00:10:33.661 --> 00:10:35.658
despite what he wants to do,

00:10:35.658 --> 00:10:38.325
my character goes and saves his.

00:10:39.732 --> 00:10:41.089
And I think that's like,

00:10:41.089 --> 00:10:42.066
it's a very simple story

00:10:42.066 --> 00:10:43.521
but it's a parable about

00:10:43.521 --> 00:10:44.557
two people just doing good

00:10:44.557 --> 00:10:45.704
despite themselves,

00:10:45.704 --> 00:10:46.894
which I love because I think

00:10:46.894 --> 00:10:49.162
you can sentimentalize doing good a lot.

00:10:49.162 --> 00:10:50.015
Like, "Oh you-"

00:10:50.015 --> 00:10:51.239
- Do what you know is right.

00:10:51.239 --> 00:10:52.072
- Yeah.

00:10:52.072 --> 00:10:53.592
And like sometimes you do it begrudgingly.

00:10:53.592 --> 00:10:54.961
Sometimes you're like, "Ugh."

00:10:54.961 --> 00:10:55.794
You know?

00:10:55.794 --> 00:10:56.754
And I love that about it,

00:10:56.754 --> 00:10:58.284
'cause I think that speaks

00:10:58.284 --> 00:11:00.190
to the best parts of us

00:11:00.190 --> 00:11:01.023
that we don't even know

00:11:01.023 --> 00:11:02.092
are the best parts of us.

00:11:02.092 --> 00:11:02.925
You know?

00:11:02.925 --> 00:11:03.989
And that's what the movie's about.

00:11:03.989 --> 00:11:06.916
- So you were into
music and music theater,

00:11:06.916 --> 00:11:07.749
and you worked

00:11:07.749 --> 00:11:09.119
with Stephen Sondheim once, right?

00:11:09.119 --> 00:11:09.952
- I did, yeah.

00:11:09.952 --> 00:11:10.921
- [Kelly] What did you do with him?

00:11:10.921 --> 00:11:12.503
- We did "Sunday in the Park with George".

00:11:12.503 --> 00:11:14.116
- [Kelly] Oh my gosh.

00:11:14.116 --> 00:11:15.844
That's so cool.

00:11:15.844 --> 00:11:17.304
(audience applauds)

00:11:17.304 --> 00:11:18.451
I love this picture.

00:11:18.451 --> 00:11:19.455
(Jake and Kelly laughing)

00:11:19.455 --> 00:11:20.774
- It literally looks
like a paparazzi fight,

00:11:20.774 --> 00:11:22.318
I'm like, "Did we work together?"

00:11:22.318 --> 00:11:23.976
Or was I trying to get a picture with him?

00:11:23.976 --> 00:11:24.972
- "Did you meet him?"

00:11:24.972 --> 00:11:25.931
- Yeah. Yeah.

00:11:25.931 --> 00:11:26.788
I'm like, "Take the picture now,

00:11:26.788 --> 00:11:28.205
he's passing by."

00:11:30.610 --> 00:11:32.448
- So you do know him.

00:11:32.448 --> 00:11:33.851
- I did know him.

00:11:33.851 --> 00:11:36.244
I think that picture
was taken opening night.

00:11:36.244 --> 00:11:38.006
Yeah, I mean,

00:11:38.006 --> 00:11:40.006
he's a legend, you know.

00:11:40.843 --> 00:11:44.492
I mean, he loved puzzles, you know,

00:11:44.492 --> 00:11:45.614
that was the most amazing thing about him.

00:11:45.614 --> 00:11:46.447
- What kind?

00:11:46.447 --> 00:11:48.061
Like putting them together or like Sudoku?

00:11:48.061 --> 00:11:49.175
- All different puzzles.

00:11:49.175 --> 00:11:50.008
- Okay, me too.

00:11:50.008 --> 00:11:50.841
I love crossword.

00:11:50.841 --> 00:11:51.674
- Yeah.

00:11:51.674 --> 00:11:52.507
He loved crosswords.

00:11:52.507 --> 00:11:53.340
But, like,

00:11:53.340 --> 00:11:54.173
any puzzle he could get his hands on,

00:11:54.173 --> 00:11:56.055
and his songs, his lyrics,

00:11:56.055 --> 00:11:57.370
and his storytelling

00:11:57.370 --> 00:11:58.453
is all like a puzzle.

00:11:58.453 --> 00:12:00.119
So like when you were performing

00:12:00.119 --> 00:12:01.112
anything he was doing,

00:12:01.112 --> 00:12:02.907
you always constantly every night

00:12:02.907 --> 00:12:05.704
trying to unpick the
puzzle for the performer

00:12:05.704 --> 00:12:06.981
as you were trying to figure it out,

00:12:06.981 --> 00:12:08.263
and then the audience was too.

00:12:08.263 --> 00:12:09.671
So there was never a night

00:12:09.671 --> 00:12:10.598
where I wasn't like,

00:12:10.598 --> 00:12:11.840
"Oh-oh, where am I going?"

00:12:11.840 --> 00:12:13.268
He's fooling you with the music.

00:12:13.268 --> 00:12:14.754
He's fooling you with the lyrics.

00:12:14.754 --> 00:12:16.065
He's playing with you.

00:12:16.065 --> 00:12:16.898
- [Kelly] Beautiful mind.

00:12:16.898 --> 00:12:17.901
- He was just an incredible man.

00:12:17.901 --> 00:12:18.963
- Yeah.

00:12:18.963 --> 00:12:20.970
That's so cool how people think like that

00:12:20.970 --> 00:12:22.108
and put things together

00:12:22.108 --> 00:12:24.547
and you can see the show a million times

00:12:24.547 --> 00:12:26.222
and come out thinking something different.

00:12:26.222 --> 00:12:27.438
- You can do it a million times.

00:12:27.438 --> 00:12:28.271
- Yeah.

00:12:28.271 --> 00:12:29.296
- The thing you realize, I think,

00:12:29.296 --> 00:12:31.218
as a performer in that space is that,

00:12:31.218 --> 00:12:33.459
you can feel so different every night,

00:12:33.459 --> 00:12:34.658
and you can add things to it,

00:12:34.658 --> 00:12:35.755
but in the end

00:12:35.755 --> 00:12:38.859
the story is always in charge, you know?

00:12:38.859 --> 00:12:40.739
It's always moving the audience.

00:12:40.739 --> 00:12:41.987
And it humbles you,

00:12:41.987 --> 00:12:42.998
'cause I think you can come out

00:12:42.998 --> 00:12:44.315
and be like, "Oh, I was so-"

00:12:44.315 --> 00:12:45.727
I remember in rehearsal once,

00:12:45.727 --> 00:12:47.212
I was rehearsing something

00:12:47.212 --> 00:12:48.540
with the other actor,

00:12:48.540 --> 00:12:49.373
and we came off stage and went,

00:12:49.373 --> 00:12:51.043
"Oh, that was the best thing we've ever-

00:12:51.043 --> 00:12:52.113
Ugh, amazing performance.

00:12:52.113 --> 00:12:53.516
Like, we just felt so connected."

00:12:53.516 --> 00:12:54.959
And the director came back and went,

00:12:54.959 --> 00:12:56.693
"That was so slow and boring."

00:12:56.693 --> 00:12:57.526
You know?

00:12:57.526 --> 00:12:58.879
- Like, just handed you some truth?

00:12:58.879 --> 00:12:59.712
- "Just speed it up.

00:12:59.712 --> 00:13:00.661
Just tell the story."

00:13:00.661 --> 00:13:01.742
And the next night we were like,

00:13:01.742 --> 00:13:02.701
"Just shave five minutes off,

00:13:02.701 --> 00:13:04.147
speed up the pace and let's go."

00:13:04.147 --> 00:13:04.980
And we did

00:13:04.980 --> 00:13:05.970
and we felt so weird about it,

00:13:05.970 --> 00:13:07.391
and she came back weeping

00:13:07.391 --> 00:13:08.481
at the end after that.

00:13:08.481 --> 00:13:09.373
- Isn't it weird?

00:13:09.373 --> 00:13:10.946
- The way in which as a performer

00:13:10.946 --> 00:13:13.060
what you feel is not always

00:13:13.060 --> 00:13:14.737
what you guys feel

00:13:14.737 --> 00:13:16.974
so incredible as an experience.

00:13:16.974 --> 00:13:18.062
It's so humbling.

00:13:18.062 --> 00:13:18.895
Like, to me.

00:13:18.895 --> 00:13:19.728
- And it's different every time,

00:13:19.728 --> 00:13:20.561
that's what I love about it.

00:13:20.561 --> 00:13:21.394
You've actually been

00:13:21.394 --> 00:13:22.990
in quite a few music videos as well,

00:13:22.990 --> 00:13:24.765
so I have to ask you, like,

00:13:24.765 --> 00:13:25.717
how did you end up,

00:13:25.717 --> 00:13:26.599
this is amazing,

00:13:26.599 --> 00:13:27.432
you were in "Blame It"

00:13:27.432 --> 00:13:28.744
with Jamie Foxx and T-Pain.

00:13:28.744 --> 00:13:29.577
How did that-?

00:13:29.577 --> 00:13:31.397
What was that, like-?

00:13:31.397 --> 00:13:32.357
Did they just call you?

00:13:32.357 --> 00:13:33.597
- [Jake] I have no idea, Kelly.

00:13:33.597 --> 00:13:35.511
I don't know how I got into that.

00:13:35.511 --> 00:13:36.371
- This is incredible.

00:13:36.371 --> 00:13:37.545
- Jamie Foxx, you know,

00:13:37.545 --> 00:13:38.378
he's like-

00:13:38.378 --> 00:13:39.211
- I love Jamie.

00:13:39.211 --> 00:13:40.044
- He's so great.

00:13:40.044 --> 00:13:41.028
And he just called me up,

00:13:41.028 --> 00:13:41.861
and he was like,

00:13:41.861 --> 00:13:44.446
"I clearly was at a
loss of finding people."

00:13:44.446 --> 00:13:46.434
I was like, probably last.

00:13:46.434 --> 00:13:47.386
I was like-

